{"chunk_id": "course-catalog-2026-1--pdf--1학기 수강편람_20260213--p135", "document_id": "course-catalog-2026-1", "document_title": "2026-1학기 수강편람 및 강의시간표 안내", "chunk_title": "A.    General         Information             on     Courses", "category": "수강", "publication_date": "2026-01-23", "applicable_year": "2026학년도 1학기", "applicable_semester": "1", "target_population": "2026-1 수강 예정 학부생", "validity_period": null, "application_period": null, "status": "expired", "status_reason": "2026-1학기 안내·신청 기간이 종료됨", "original_filename": "course-catalog-2026-1__2026-1학기 수강편람_20260213.pdf", "file_type": "PDF", "source_url": "https://www.sejong.ac.kr/kor/intro/notice3.do?articleNo=862579&mode=view", "source_location": "PDF 원본 p.135", "page_number": 135, "section": "A.    General         Information             on     Courses", "chunk_body": "A.    General         Information             on     Courses\n\nA-1.  Names of Categories       in the   General Education Curriculum\n                         Category                                                 Category Field                           Abbr.\n        Korean                       English                      Korean                         English\n     공통교양필수               Required Common Courses                이수영역 지정 없음 / No               assigned   category         공필\n                                                                역사와사상                    History  and Thought\n                                                                자연과과학                    Nature and Science\n     균형교양필수               Required Balanced Courses             경제와사회                   Economy     and Society            균필\n                                                                문화와예술                      Culture and Arts\n                                                                융합과창의                Convergence and      Creativity\n   학문기초교양필수              Basic Science   &  Mathematics          이수영역 지정 없음 / No               assigned   category         기필\n                                                                사상과역사                    Thought and History\n                                                                사회와문화                    Society and Culture\n       교양선택                  Liberal Arts:  Electives        자연과과학기술                   Nature and    Technology            교선\n                                                                예술과체육                       Arts and Sports\n                                                               세계와지구촌              World and     Global Community\n                                                             자기계발과진로                Self-development and Career\n\n\nA-2.  Limitation  in Retaking    Courses\n  Students may retake up to         3  courses   per  semester.    However, students who have exceeded the standard\n  number of semesters(students taking extra semesters) and students that have                      received a score of     F\n  (including   FA,  NP, I) do not have a       limit in  the number of      courses   that can be retaken per semester.\n  (Clause 6, Article 10,    Sejong    University’s  Regulations    on Academic      Affairs)\n\nA-3.  Changes in    the Limits for    Absences\n  a. Students will    receive an FA if they are absent         for more    than or equal to 1/4 of the total number of\n     classes during     the semester(Clause 1, Article 53, Sejong          University’s Regulations on Academic Affairs)\n     Ex) Students will receive       an  FA if  they  are  absent 4 or     more out of 16      classes  or 8 or more out of\n         32 classes.\n  b. For   courses that    have experiments and practice sessions, or that            have online-offline hybrid learning,\n     students who receive        an FA   in any one of these categories, will         receive an FA grade       for the entire\n     course(Clause     2,  Article 53, Sejong University’s Regulations         on  Academic Affairs).\n  c. For  online   courses,  if more than 1/4 of the        total number of      course content has not been watched,\n     the   course   is treated as   an FA(Clause 3, Article 53, Sejong         University’s   Regulations on Academic\n     Affairs).\n\nA-4.  Lecture  Hours\n  a. “75-minute Lecture”\n    - A 3-credit course(150-minute lectures and a             30-minute     break per week)      will be  divided into\n       two 75-minute lectures.\n    - In  the lecture schedule,      sessions are indicated as 90 minutes per session,             for example,\n       “Monday 10:30-12:00”(75-minute-lectures/15-minute-break).\n      Year    Course   No.    Category          Course          Class   Credit(s)    Lecture Hours       Lecture    Instructor\n                                                                                                          Room\n        1       DGC251         Elective     Korean Culture       001        3      M/W    1030-12:00      광102\n                                             and Society\n\n  b. Policies  regarding “75-minute Lecture” courses\n    - Courses on schedules will         be shown     in “hours”, not “periods”.\n    - Courses do      not  only  start not on the hour       but  also at half   past(30   minutes    after) the hour.\n  c. Courses    that have classes for     1  hour,  2  consecutive hours, and 3 consecutive           hours  must    specify  their\n     hours, including break       times(50   minutes    of lecture/10 minutes      of break)    in formats   such   as\n     “Mon 09:00-10:00/Mon          09:00-11:00/Mon      09:00-12:00”.\n\n\n\n\n                                                             -  135 -\n\n[구조화 표 1: 원래 행·열 순서 보존; 병합 셀은 null일 수 있음]\nROW 1: Category | null | Category Field | null | Abbr.\nROW 2: Korean | English | Korean | English | null\nROW 3: 공통교양필수 | Required Common Courses | 이수영역 지정 없음 / No assigned category | null | 공필\nROW 4: 균형교양필수 | Required Balanced Cours