{"chunk_id": "tuition-registration-2026-1--pdf- Year (Undergrads)--p001", "document_id": "tuition-registration-2026-1", "document_title": "2026-1 학부 재학생 등록금 납부 안내", "chunk_title": "2026         Academic               Year        (Undergrads)", "category": "학생지원", "publication_date": "2026-02-03", "applicable_year": "2026학년도 1학기", "applicable_semester": "1", "target_population": "학부 재학생·복학생·재입학생 및 초과학기자", "validity_period": null, "application_period": "2026-02-23", "status": "expired", "status_reason": "2026-1학기 안내·신청 기간이 종료됨", "original_filename": "tuition-registration-2026-1__Guide to Registration in the 1st Semester of the 2026 Academic Year (Undergrads).pdf", "file_type": "PDF", "source_url": "https://www.sejong.ac.kr/kor/intro/notice1.do?articleNo=863049&mode=view", "source_location": "PDF 원본 p.1", "page_number": 1, "section": "2026         Academic               Year        (Undergrads)", "chunk_body": "Guide          to     Registration                in     the     1st      Semester             of     the\n\n                   2026         Academic               Year        (Undergrads)\n\n\n\n\n\nThis  is to  guide   the  registration   process   for the  1st  semester    of the  academic     year  of  2026.\n\nPlease  register  within   the  registration  period   to  proceed   your   studies  at  Sejong   University.\n\n\n\n\nⅠ.   Registration       Details    (Current      Students)\n\n1. Registration    Period\n 1) Date:    Feb  23th   (Mon)    ~  26th   (Thu)\n\n 2) Office   hours:   AM    9  ~   PM   4  (Banks’   office  hours)\n\n    ※Transfer    Possible   hours:   AM    9  ~  PM    5\n\n\n\n2. Registration    Methods\n\n 1) Payment     by  visiting  banks:   Branches    of  Kookmin      Bank   and   NH    Bank   across   the\n\n county\n\n 2) Account     transfer\n\n  -  Please   check   the  account:    account   numbers     of Kookmin      bank   on  the  payment     bill\n\n     (one-time    accounts    that  cannot   be   reused)\n\n  -  Account number:        It is a  temporary     account   with   the  student’s   name,   set  as the\n\n    individual   holder  of  the  account.    Please  make    sure  to  process the    transfer  after  checking\n\n    whether   the  cost  and   the  account    holder   (student’s  name)    are  accurate.\n\n※  It  is a  one-time    temporary     individual   account   for  the  receipt   of registration   fees  (tuition\n\nfees). Therefore    it will be  automatically     registered  once   the  payment     is made.\n\n※   If you    are  using   international    wire-transfer,    Please   choose    local  currency,    KRW,     and\n\nadd   bank   fees.  Otherwise,     your   transfer   may    be  rejected   due   to  incorrect   amount     being\n\ntransferred   to your   designated    account.\n\n※   Numbers     next   to  Nonghyup       Bank   are   the  university   code   that  the   banks   use   for  the\n\ndeposit process.\n\n※Voluntary      fees  (Student    Union    fees,  Alumni    fees)   cannot    be  paid   individually    so  it  is\n\nrecommended      to  pay   supplement    fees  along with     the  tuition  fees.", "structured_tables": [], "retrieval_allowed": true, "default_searchable": true, "quality_flags": ["pdf_text_extracted"], "pdf_page_count": 6, "embedded_image_count": 0, "evaluation_academic_year": 2026, "evaluation_semester": 1}
{"chunk_id": "tuition-registration-2026-1--pdf- Year (Undergrads)--p002", "document_id": "tuition-registration-2026-1", "document_title": "2026-1 학부 재학생 등록금 납부 안내", "chunk_title": "[ Things     to  Note     When     Making       International      Wire    Transfers     ]", "category": "학생지원", "publication_date": "2026-02-03", "applicable_year": "2026학년도 1학기", "applicable_semester": "1", "target_population": "학부 재학생·복학생·재입학생 및 초과학기자", "validity_period": null, "application_period": "2026-02-23", "status": "expired", "status_reason": "2026-1학기 안내·신청 기간이 종료됨", "original_filename": "tuition-registration-2026-1__Guide to Registration in the 1st Semester of the 2026 Academic Year (Undergrads).pdf", "file_type": "PDF", "source_url": "https://www.sejong.ac.kr/kor/intro/notice1.do?articleNo=863049&mode=view", "source_location": "PDF 원본 p.2", "page_number": 2, "section": "[ Things     to  Note     When     Making       International      Wire    Transfers     ]", "chunk_body": "[ Things     to  Note     When     Making       International      Wire    Transfers     ]\n\n\nA.   International     wire    transfers     can    take   considerable      time    to   be    confirmed      due    to\nverification   processes    by  the  sending    country,    intermediary     banks,   and    other  institutions.\nPlease   be   aware    that   even    if you    send   an   international     wire   transfer    within    the  tuition\npayment      period,    your    registration    may     not   be    completed      if  domestic     confirmation       is\ndelayed.\n\n\nB.  When      making     an    international     wire   transfer,    you    must    take    into   account     all  fees\ncharged    in each   country    and    by  each   bank    involved.\n\n\nC.  You    must    verify  your    own    virtual   account    number     for   the  relevant    semester    and   send\nthe  funds   to  that  account.\n\n\nD.  If  you   send   less  than    the  required    amount,     your    registration    will  not   be  processed.     If\nyou   send   more    than    the  required    amount,      the  excess    will  be   refunded    to   the  originating\ninternational    account.     However,      if  the   overpaid     amount      is  too   small    to  be   reasonably\nrefunded,    a return   or   refund   may    not  be   possible.\n\n\n☆   Please   note   that   if  you   send   your    tuition   in  any   of  the   following     ways,   the   payment\nwill  not    be   processed     and    the   funds    will   be   returned    to   the   originating     international\naccount.   ☆\n\n\nA.  The   funds   are   sent  to  a  virtual  account     other   than   your   virtual  account    for   the  relevant\nsemester.\nB. The    international    wire   transfer   is made    under   a  name    other   than   your    own.\nC.  Sejong   University    is not   specified   as  the  beneficiary    (recipient).\n\n\n\n\n\n\n[ Tuition     payment      through     private    currency     exchange      services    is  strictly  prohibited      ]\n\n\n\nDue   to  repeated    voice   phishing    incidents   each   semester    involving    tuition  payments     to  virtual\naccounts,    tuition  payments     made    through     any   third  party,   including    private   currency\nexchange    agencies,    are  strictly  prohibited.    If an  account     hold   or  payment     suspension     occurs\nbecause    tuition  was   paid   by   a third   party   under   another    person’s    name,    that  payment     will\nbe deemed      invalid  and   the   student   will  be  required    to  repay   the  tuition.\n\n[구조화 표 1: 원래 행·열 순서 보존; 병합 셀은 null일 수 있음]\nROW 1: [ Tuition payment through private currency exchange services is strictly prohibited | ]\n\n[구조화 표 2: 원래 행·열 순서 보존; 병합 셀은 null일 수 있음]\nROW 1: accounts, tuition payments made through any third party, including private currency | null\n\n[구조화 표 3: 원래 행·열 순서 보존; 병합 셀은 null일 수 있음]\nROW 1: because tuition was paid by a third party under another person’s name, that payment will | null", "structured_tables": [[["[ Tuition payment through private currency exchange services is strictly prohibited", "]"]], [["accounts, tuition payments made through any third party, including private currency", null]], [["because tuition was paid by a third party under another person’s name, that payment will", null]]], "retrieval_allowed": true, "default_searchable": true, "quality_flags": ["pdf_text_extracted", "tables_detected"], "pdf_page_count": 6, "embedded_image_count": 0, "evaluation_academic_year": 2026, "evaluation_semester": 1}
