ine  credits   1/2  of  the   tuition  fees  for  the  current    semester\n\n\n\n3. Registration     fees  for  a  student    who    has  exceeded     the  regular   semesters    will   be  issued   as\n\npayment     bills in  accordance     with   the registered     credits.\n\nFor   those   you   are   about    to  take   an   extra   semester    will   be  able   to  find   their   bills from\n\n20th   of  Feb.   Make     sure   you   pay   off  your    tuition   when    you   finish   your   course    selection,\n\nmeaning     you   will   more    likely   pay   your    bill during    extended     period.    If  any   changes     are\n\nmade    to  the  list of  credits   registered   after  the   issue  of  the  payment     bill,   please   visit  Dept.\n\nof   Financial    Affairs.    Dept.    of   Financial     Affairs    will   provide     a   revised    copy     of   the\n\npayment/tuition      bill.\n\nAll  students     who     should    take    extra    semester     will  be    processed     only    at   branches     of\n\nKookmin      Bank(the    use  of  one-time     account     is also  possible.)\n\n\nⅢ.    A   student      who     has    won      full  scholarships        or   has    received      0   won     notice\n\n(on   the    bill)\n\n    1.  If  you   are   paying    Voluntary      Expenses     –   Either    visit branches     of   Kookmin      Bank,\n\nNonghyup      Bank    across   the  county    or  use   the  Kookmin      Bank    one-time     account    to  register.\n\n\n\n  2.  If you   do   not   want   to  pay   Voluntary     Expenses-      Visit  branches    of  Kookmin      Bank    and\n\nrequest that    it will  be  processed as      a  0  won   registration\n\nIf no   payment     is  made    on   the  day    of  your   request,   your    status   on  portal   will   remain    as\n\n‘Unregistered’.    Please   check   if  your   request   for   0  won    registration   is  processed    by   going   to", "structured_tables": [], "retrieval_allowed": true, "default_searchable": true, "quality_flags": ["pdf_text_extracted"], "pdf_page_count": 6, "embedded_image_count": 0, "evaluation_academic_year": 2026, "evaluation_semester": 1}
