 Possible  date   of printing   payment    bill and   Payment     Period\n\n\n            Possible   date  of  printing   payment    bill                   Payment    Period\n                                                                 (in full compliance with the payment period)\n   1st                      Mar    06th  ~                              Mar   11  ~   13  (Wed~Fri)\n   2nd                       Apr   01th ~                               Apr   08  ~  10   (Wed~Fri)\n   3rd                       Apr   29th ~                               May   06   ~  08  (Wed~Fri)\n   4th                      May    27th  ~                        Jun   02,  04  ~  05   (Tue,Wed~Thu)\n\n\n\n4. How    to  check   whether    you   have  applied   for  Split Payments\n\nSejong  portal   Academic     Information    >  장학/등록        및  학생지원        >  등록이력조회           > 분납여부\nIf your  split  payment    application   is accepted,    You   can  check   \"Y\"\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n\n※Print-out     of Payment     Bill:\n\nSejong  portal    Academic     Information    >  장학/등록        및   학생지원       >  등록이력조회\n\n[구조화 표 1: 원래 행·열 순서 보존; 병합 셀은 null일 수 있음]\nROW 1: null | Possible date of printing payment bill | Payment Period (in full compliance with the payment period)\nROW 2: 1st | Mar 06th ~ | Mar 11 ~ 13 (Wed~Fri)\nROW 3: 2nd | Apr 01th ~ | Apr 08 ~ 10 (Wed~Fri)\nROW 4: 3rd | Apr 29th ~ | May 06 ~ 08 (Wed~Fri)\nROW 5: 4th | May 27th ~ | Jun 02, 04 ~ 05 (Tue,Wed~Thu)", "structured_tables": [[[null, "Possible date of printing payment bill", "Payment Period (in full compliance with the payment period)"], ["1st", "Mar 06th ~", "Mar 11 ~ 13 (Wed~Fri)"], ["2nd", "Apr 01th ~", "Apr 08 ~ 10 (Wed~Fri)"], ["3rd", "Apr 29th ~", "May 06 ~ 08 (Wed~Fri)"], ["4th", "May 27th ~", "Jun 02, 04 ~ 05 (Tue,Wed~Thu)"]]], "retrieval_allowed": true, "default_searchable": true, "quality_flags": ["pdf_text_extracted", "tables_detected"], "pdf_page_count": 6, "embedded_image_count": 1, "evaluation_academic_year": 2026, "evaluation_semester": 1}
{"chunk_id": "tuition-registration-2026-1--pdf- Year (Undergrads)--p005", "document_id": "tuition-registration-2026-1", "document_title": "2026-1 학부 재학생 등록금 납부 안내", "chunk_title": "※   Available   for  printing   after    possible   date  of  printing   payment bill", "category": "학생지원", "publication_date": "2026-02-03", "applicable_year": "2026학년도 1학기", "applicable_semester": "1", "target_population": "학부 재학생·복학생·재입학생 및 초과학기자", "validity_period": null, "application_period": "2026-02-23", "status": "expired", "status_reason": "2026-1학기 안내·신청 기간이 종료됨", "original_filename": "tuition-registration-2026-1__Guide to Registration in the 1st Semester of the 2026 Academic Year (Undergrads).pdf", "file_type": "PDF", "source_url": "https://www.sejong.ac.kr/kor/intro/notice1.do?articleNo=863049&mode=view", "source_location": "PDF 원본 p.5", "page_number": 5, "section": "※   Available   for  printing   after    possible   date  of  printing   payment bill", "chunk_body": "※   Available   for  printing   after    possible   date  of  printing   payment bill\n\n※   1,2,3,4   round    of   payment     for   one-time     accounts    may    differ   from    each   other.   Please\n\nmake   sure   to  double-check      the  account    numbers     upon    payment     of each   round.\n\n\nⅤ.   De-Registration           and    automatic       removal\n\n If  a  student    fails  to  pay    the  tuition   during    the   announced      period    it  will  lead   to   the\n\nautomatic     removal    from    the   registration    (as  unregistered)     and   grades    obtained     from    the\n\ncurrent   semester   are  not   regarded    as  officially  earned.\n\n\nⅥ.   Applicants       for   government         student      loans\n\n As   differences   in   loans   may    occur   due   to   split  payments,     students   who    wish    to  benefit\n\nfrom   government      student   loans   should   not  apply    for  split payment.\n\n(A  student   who    has   applied   for  split payment     and   government      student   loans   will  be  unable\n\nto pay)\n\n\nⅦ.   Notes\n\n1.  If records    indicated    on   the   certificates   already   issued    are  different   from    your    current\n\nstatus  due   to  a leave   of  absence    or  removal    from   the   registration(also    used   for  the  issue  of\na  passport    or  for   training   as  reserves   forces),   it  is the   student’s   responsibility    to   fix  the\n\ndifferences.\n\n2. Refund     policies  due   to  a  leave   of  absence    or  voluntary     withdrawal:     With    adherence     to\n\nArticle  63  of  the  University    Constitution     Amendment       refund   will  be  calculated.    ( deduct    the\n\nsame   amount     from   the  full-paid    tuition  payers)\n\n\nⅧ..   Contact      Numbers         :  for   inquiries     (Korean      Language)\n\nRegistration:    02-3408-3022        (Dept.   of  Financial   Affairs)\n\nScholarships    :  02-3408-3054       (the   Office   of Student    Affairs)\n\nNational    Grant   :  02-3408-4355        (the  Office   of  Student   Affairs)\n\nGovernment      student   loan   :  02-3408-6056       (the   Office  of  Student    Affairs)", "structured_tables": [], "retrieval_allowed": true, "default_searchable": true, "quality_flags": ["pdf_text_extracted"], "pdf_page_count": 6, "embedded_image_count": 1, "evaluation_academic_year": 2026, "evaluation_semester": 1}
